config DOOR_LOCK_GESTURE_ACCESS_MODEL
	bool "Gesture access inference model (direct Nordic Axon FOMO)"
	select CPP
	select NRF_AXON
	help
	  Builds a 96x96 grayscale FOMO object detector using the Nordic Axon
	  NPU directly. Camera bytes are quantized to int8 without a float
	  feature matrix, and FOMO output is decoded locally without the Edge
	  Impulse runtime. Selected automatically by
	  CONFIG_DOOR_LOCK_GESTURE_ACCESS; do not enable directly.

	  The model itself is named generically ("fomo", not tied to any one
	  export) so a weights-only retrain with the same tensor and
	  quantization contract is a drop-in replacement.

if DOOR_LOCK_GESTURE_ACCESS_MODEL

config NRF_AXON_INTERLAYER_BUFFER_SIZE
	int
	default 120000
	help
	  The current "fomo" model needs 119808 bytes of interlayer buffer
	  space (NRF_AXON_MODEL_FOMO_MAX_IL_BUFFER_USED in
	  nordic-axon-model/nrf_axon_model_fomo_.h); rounded up here with a
	  small margin. CONFIG_NRF_AXON_INTERLAYER_BUFFER_SIZE defaults to 0
	  upstream and the model header hard-asserts on it being too small,
	  so this must be set for the model to link/run at all.

	  Only needs to change here if a future model swap changes the
	  architecture (layer shapes/count) enough to need a different
	  amount - a same-architecture, weights-only retrain (the case this
	  project is set up for) needs the exact same buffer size, since that
	  size depends on layer shapes, not weight values.

endif # DOOR_LOCK_GESTURE_ACCESS_MODEL

# Swapping in a new model
# ------------------------
# This project is deliberately set up so that swapping in a retrained model
# - same architecture (FOMO), same 96x96 grayscale input, different weights
# - is a drop-in file replacement, nothing else:
#   1. Overwrite subsys/gesture_access/model/nordic-axon-model/nrf_axon_model_fomo_.h
#      with the new export's Axon model header - but renamed to that exact
#      filename, and with every occurrence of whatever model name Edge
#      Impulse assigned at export time (e.g. jfda_detection_26,
#      MY_PROJECT_v2, ...) replaced with "fomo", both lowercase (struct/
#      array names, e.g. model_jfda_detection_26 -> model_fomo) and
#      uppercase (macro constants, e.g.
#      NRF_AXON_MODEL_JFDA_DETECTION_26_MAX_IL_BUFFER_USED ->
#      NRF_AXON_MODEL_FOMO_MAX_IL_BUFFER_USED). This is a pure
#      find-and-replace of one token, safe to script
#      (sed -i 's/OLD_NAME/fomo/g; s/OLD_NAME_UPPER/FOMO/g' ...).
#   2. Keep the 96x96x1 input, 12x12x2 output, input/output quantization,
#      class order, and "hand" label contract unchanged. The direct runtime
#      validates these values during initialization.
#   3. Only revisit CONFIG_NRF_AXON_INTERLAYER_BUFFER_SIZE above if the new
#      export's ..._MAX_IL_BUFFER_USED constant is larger than the current
#      120000 default - shouldn't happen for a weights-only retrain of the
#      same architecture.
